+      this repository counts, ``_nested_binding`` binds its own HEAD and delta,
+      so the outer delta must NOT also cover it. Returning normally means "skip
+      this entry, it is already covered";
+    * undeclared -- refuse, naming the exact contract that is missing. A nested
+      repository is never silently included, excluded or modified: it needs an
+      ownership decision, and this message is the actionable path to it;
+    * anything else Git claims is a directory boundary (a reparse point, a
+      directory that is not a Git work tree root, a path that escapes the
+      project) stays fatal, unchanged.
